('75', '0', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Delivery Format Matters for Nursing Students</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Nursing is a hands-on profession, yet a growing share of U.S. nursing programs deliver some or all didactic coursework online. The debate between online and campus nursing programs is not about whether clinical training exists - every accredited program requires supervised patient care - but about how theory is taught, how clinicals are scheduled, and how well the format fits your life.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Campus programs traditionally combine in-person lectures, skills labs, simulation, and clinical rotations in a structured weekly schedule. Online and hybrid programs replace or reduce classroom seat time with digital modules, live virtual sessions, and periodic on-campus intensives. Both models can produce licensure-ready graduates when accreditation, faculty qualifications, and clinical partnerships meet national standards.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Your choice should reflect sustainable habits. An online program that looks flexible on paper can fail if you lack reliable internet, quiet study time, or proximity to clinical sites. A campus program that looks immersive can strain a household if commuting and fixed class times conflict with employment. Compare formats against your real weekly calendar, not an ideal one.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Clinical Requirements: What Online Programs Still Demand</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>No reputable online nursing program eliminates clinical practice. State boards of nursing and accrediting bodies require hundreds of supervised clinical hours for RN and BSN candidates. Online students complete rotations at approved healthcare facilities - often near their home communities - while completing coursework digitally.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Ask each program how clinical sites are assigned. Some institutions maintain regional placement teams; others expect students to propose sites subject to approval. Understand travel radius, shift timing, and whether weekend or evening clinicals are available for working students.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Campus programs may offer more predictable placement through long-standing hospital partnerships but less flexibility in scheduling. Online programs may offer more asynchronous coursework yet require you to adapt when a clinical site assigns overnight or weekday shifts. Clarify these details before enrollment to avoid surprises mid-program.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:hlm/article-compare {\"headline\":\"Flexibility, Pace, and Student Support\",\"leftTitle\":\"Online u0026 Hybrid Programs\",\"rightTitle\":\"Campus Programs\",\"leftParagraphs\":[\"Online nursing programs appeal to working adults across the United States who need to complete weekly modules after shifts or during lunch breaks. Many use cohort models with weekly deadlines rather than fully self-paced structures, preserving accountability while allowing geographic freedom.\",\"Online programs increasingly offer virtual office hours, remote simulation, and dedicated student success coaches to replicate support at a distance.\"],\"rightParagraphs\":[\"Campus programs provide immediate access to faculty office hours, peer study groups, and on-site simulation labs. Students who learn best through in-person demonstration and spontaneous questions may thrive in that environment.\",\"They may also provide stronger on-campus career fairs and alumni networks in the institution\'s region.\"],\"footnote\":[\"Evaluate support services with equal rigor: tutoring, NCLEX preparation, mental health resources, and academic advising. Nursing curricula are rigorous; the format that includes proactive coaching often predicts completion better than the format with the lowest advertised tuition.\"]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Employer Perception and Career Outcomes</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>U.S. hospital hiring practices have shifted as accredited online nursing degrees became common at established universities. Employers typically verify accreditation, NCLEX pass rates, and clinical competence during hiring rather than rejecting candidates based solely on online coursework.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Regional reputation still matters. A campus program with deep ties to local health systems may streamline recruitment in that market. An online program affiliated with a respected university can carry similar weight when clinical partners and alumni placements are strong.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Focus on outcomes data: graduate employment rates, employer partnerships, and specialty placement if you target specific units such as ICU, pediatrics, or community health. Format matters less than whether the program consistently places graduates where you want to work.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Compare Total Cost and Hidden Expenses</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Tuition per credit hour is only part of the financial picture. Campus programs may add housing, parking, and commuting costs. Online programs may include technology fees, travel to on-campus intensives, and clinical uniforms or equipment. Build a full budget for each option you consider.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Time-to-degree affects earnings. A campus ADN program completed in two years may get you into the workforce faster than a part-time online BSN spread across six years - or the reverse if an accelerated online bridge fits your prior credits. Model salary impact using realistic graduation timelines.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Financial aid rules apply similarly to accredited online and campus programs at participating institutions. Submit the FAFSA, compare award letters, and ask about scholarships for healthcare majors or returning adult students.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:hlm/article-callout {\"variant\":\"help\",\"headline\":\"Make the Decision That Keeps You on Track to Licensure\",\"paragraphs\":[\"Online and campus nursing programs both lead to meaningful careers when you choose accredited pathways aligned with your state licensure requirements. Prioritize CCNE or ACEN accreditation, transparent NCLEX outcomes, and clinical placement support - then select the delivery model you can maintain through graduation.\",\"If you want help comparing nursing pathways and connecting with accredited partner institutions, Higher Learning Marketers supports prospective students with program matching and enrollment guidance. Visit our u003ca href=u0022/contact-us/u0022u003econtact pageu003c/au003e or read related student resources on our blog to continue your research with confidence.\"]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:hlm/article-checklist {\"headline\":\"Questions to Ask Before You Enroll\",\"paragraphs\":[\"Use a consistent checklist when comparing programs. Request written answers from admissions rather than relying on informal conversations alone.\"],\"items\":[\"Accreditation body (CCNE or ACEN) and state authorization status\",\"Total clinical hours and skills lab requirements\",\"NCLEX pass rates by year and cohort\",\"Graduate employment rates in your target market\",\"Total cost including travel to on-campus intensives\",\"Clinical site assignment process and travel expectations\"],\"outro\":[\"Speak with current students or recent graduates when possible. Cohort culture, faculty responsiveness, and clinical placement reliability rarely appear in brochures but strongly affect completion.\",\"Confirm state authorization and licensure eligibility if you plan to practice in a state different from the program\'s primary location - especially for online pathways serving multi-state cohorts.\"]} /-->', 'Online vs Campus Nursing Programs: Which Fits Your Career?', 'Online vs campus nursing programs in the U.S. - compare clinical hours, NCLEX outcomes, flexibility, employer views, and total cost before you enroll.', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'online-vs-campus-nursing-programs', '', '', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/online-vs-campus-nursing-programs/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('76', '0', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Move Beyond Cost-Per-Lead as a Primary KPI</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Enrollment marketing ROI suffers when institutions optimize exclusively for cost-per-lead (CPL). CPL is easy to report and compare across vendors, but it ignores whether inquiries convert to applications, starts, and retained students. A low CPL campaign that produces non-responsive records can cost more per enrolled student than a higher-CPL channel with strong advisor conversion.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>U.S. universities facing enrollment pressure in nursing, business, and adult learner segments need metrics tied to revenue and mission - filled seats in high-margin programs, improved diversity goals, and sustainable cohort sizes. Marketing leaders and enrollment directors should agree on primary KPIs before budget cycles allocate spend to vanity metrics.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Cost-per-start (CPS) or cost-per-enrollment provides a stronger foundation for ROI conversations. It connects acquisition spend to the outcome that actually affects tuition revenue and utilization of instructional capacity.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Map the Full Funnel With Clean Attribution</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>ROI analysis requires stage-level tracking from first touch through orientation. Tag campaigns with consistent UTM parameters, persist lead source in your CRM or SIS integration, and resist overwriting original source when students re-engage through different channels.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Define stage criteria clearly: what counts as contacted, qualified, applied, admitted, and started. Ambiguous definitions create reporting noise that hides underperforming sources. Weekly funnel reviews with marketing and admissions present catch quality decay before terms begin under-enrolled.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Multi-touch attribution acknowledges that adult learners often research for months across search, social, email, and referrals. Even simple models - first-touch and last-touch side by side - improve decisions compared to ignoring attribution entirely.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Calculate ROI With Program-Level Economics</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Aggregate enrollment ROI can mask program-level losses. A campaign that fills an online MBA cohort profitably may simultaneously attract underqualified inquiries into a capacity-constrained nursing program with expensive clinical placement. Analyze ROI by program, modality, and geography.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Include variable costs in ROI models: advisor compensation tied to outreach, application processing, financial aid packaging, and melt reduction campaigns. Fixed marketing spend is only part of the enrollment cost structure.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Where data allows, extend analysis to student lifetime value - retention, upsell to graduate programs, and alumni giving for traditional-age populations. Short-term start metrics matter most for immediate budget decisions, but lifetime frames inform strategic investments in brand and content.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Improve ROI Through Lead Quality and Speed-to-Contact</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Higher-intent inquiries convert at higher rates, which lowers effective CPS even when CPL rises. Content hubs, transparent consent flows, and program-specific landing pages attract students further along the decision journey than generic lead forms.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Advisor response time is an ROI lever. Studies across U.S. education markets consistently show decay in contact rates after the first hour. Automate routing, staff peak inquiry windows, and measure conversion by response-time bands.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Partnerships with consent-based providers such as Higher Learning Marketers can improve ROI when inquiries include documented opt-in and program match data. Review our <a href=\"/services/\">university lead generation services</a> and compare downstream start rates against current vendors.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Report ROI to Stakeholders With Context</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Executive dashboards should pair CPS with volume, mix, and capacity utilization - not isolated percentages. A rising CPS during a deliberate shift toward adult learners may reflect acceptable economics if those students persist at higher rates.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Benchmark internally year over year and against peer groups where available. External CPL benchmarks without program context mislead leadership. Tell stories with cohort data: which channels produced students who persisted to credit-hour milestones.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Document tests and learnings. ROI improvement compounds when institutions reinvest savings from pruned channels into content, conversion rate optimization, and advisor training.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Build a Sustainable Enrollment Marketing Engine</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Enrollment marketing ROI is not a one-time audit - it is an operating discipline linking creative, media, technology, and admissions. Institutions that align KPIs, attribution, and quality feedback loops reduce wasted spend while filling priority programs more predictably.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you want help connecting marketing investment to starts through consent-based inquiry generation, <a href=\"/contact-us/\">request a consultation with Higher Learning Marketers</a>. We partner with U.S. universities to deliver measurable enrollment outcomes, not just lead volume.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Scenario Planning for Enrollment Budgets</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Model best-, expected-, and worst-case start scenarios tied to marketing spend before terms begin. Scenario planning forces explicit assumptions about conversion rates by channel rather than hoping last year\'s funnel repeats.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Include melt between admit and start in worst-case models - especially for adult learners facing work or childcare disruptions close to term start.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Share scenarios with finance and academic leadership so enrollment targets align with instructional capacity and revenue planning.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Common ROI Pitfalls to Avoid</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Avoid comparing CPL across programs with different price points and conversion economics. A graduate program with long research cycles cannot be judged by the same weekly dashboards as a certificate campaign.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Do not ignore organic inquiry value when evaluating paid ROI. Brand investment lifts all channels; isolating paid-only metrics undervalues content and SEO that reduce marginal CPL over time.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Document vendor changes and creative tests so year-over-year ROI shifts are explainable - not mistaken for market noise.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Enrollment Marketing ROI: What Universities Should Measure', 'Enrollment marketing ROI for U.S. universities - measure cost-per-start, funnel attribution, and program economics instead of chasing cost-per-lead alone.', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'enrollment-marketing-roi-for-universities', '', '', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/enrollment-marketing-roi-for-universities/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('77', '0', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '<h2>Understanding Your Nursing Pathway Options</h2><p>Choosing the right nursing program is one of the most important decisions in your healthcare career. Whether you are exploring an RN diploma, a BSN, or an MSN for career advancement, the right fit depends on your schedule, budget, licensure goals, and long-term specialty interests.</p><h2>Compare Program Types</h2><p>RN programs offer the fastest route to licensure. BSN programs build broader leadership and research skills valued by major hospital systems. MSN programs suit nurses targeting advanced practice, education, or administration roles.</p><h2>Evaluate Accreditation and Outcomes</h2><p>Prioritize CCNE- or ACEN-accredited programs with strong NCLEX pass rates and clinical placement support. Ask about graduate employment rates before you apply.</p>', 'How to Choose the Right Nursing Program', 'A practical guide for students comparing RN, BSN, and MSN pathways across campus and online options.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '37-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '', '37', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=77', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('78', '0', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '<h2>Volume Is Not the Same as Enrollment Intent</h2><p>Universities investing in paid acquisition often measure success by lead volume. But enrollment outcomes depend on lead quality: intent, fit, consent, and timeliness. A smaller pool of qualified inquiries consistently outperforms bulk lists with weak conversion.</p><h2>What Defines a Quality Education Lead</h2><p>High-quality leads include verified contact information, explicit consent, program-interest match, and readiness indicators such as start-date preference and prior education level.</p><h2>Building a Quality-First Funnel</h2><p>Pair targeted content hubs with multi-step forms, clear privacy disclosures, and rapid advisor follow-up. Institutions that align marketing KPIs with enrollment KPIs reduce cost-per-start and improve student satisfaction.</p>', 'What Universities Should Know About Lead Quality', 'Why pre-qualified, consent-based inquiries outperform raw volume in enrollment marketing.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '38-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '', '38', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=78', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('79', '0', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '<h2>Applying as a Working Adult</h2><p>Working adults face unique application constraints: limited evening hours, transcript retrieval delays, and uncertainty about credit for prior learning. A structured plan keeps your application on track without overwhelming your schedule.</p><h2>Prepare Documents Early</h2><p>Gather transcripts, employment history, and professional references before you begin. Many career-focused programs prioritize work experience alongside academic history.</p><h2>Write a Purpose-Driven Statement</h2><p>Connect your current role to your target degree. Admissions teams want to see clear career intent, not just a generic interest in further study.</p>', 'Berkeley College Application Tips for Working Adults', 'How to prepare a strong application when balancing work, family, and career-focused education.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '39-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '', '39', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=79', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('80', '0', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '<h2>Flexibility vs Immersion</h2><p>Online nursing programs appeal to working professionals who need schedule flexibility. Campus programs provide structured clinical rotations and in-person faculty access. Your learning style and life constraints should drive the decision.</p><h2>Clinical Requirements Matter</h2><p>Every credible nursing program includes supervised clinical hours. Compare how each format places students with local healthcare partners and whether clinical scheduling fits your work calendar.</p><h2>Evaluate Employer Perception</h2><p>Accredited online and campus degrees from reputable institutions carry similar licensure outcomes. Focus on accreditation, NCLEX pass rates, and employer partnerships rather than delivery format alone.</p>', 'Online vs Campus Nursing Programs: Which Fits Your Career?', 'Compare online and campus-based nursing pathways by cost, clinical requirements, flexibility, and career outcomes.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '75-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '', '75', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=80', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('81', '0', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '<h2>Move Beyond Cost-Per-Lead</h2><p>Enrollment leaders often track CPL and application volume. ROI improves when you connect marketing spend to starts, retention, and program margin. Cost-per-start is a stronger primary KPI than raw inquiry counts.</p><h2>Attribute Across the Funnel</h2><p>Use UTM parameters, CRM stage tracking, and source-level reporting to understand which channels produce students who persist. High-intent content hubs typically outperform broad paid campaigns on start rate.</p><h2>Optimize With Quality Signals</h2><p>Integrate lead quality scoring, advisor response time, and conversion by program. Institutions that review weekly funnel data reduce wasted spend and improve partnership conversations with agencies.</p>', 'Enrollment Marketing ROI: What Universities Should Measure', 'How to measure enrollment marketing ROI beyond lead volume — from cost-per-start to lifetime student value.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '76-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '2026-06-16 20:37:23', '', '76', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=81', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('82', '0', '2026-06-16 20:49:31', '2026-06-16 20:49:31', '<h2>Why Education SEO Is Different</h2><p>Generic SEO chases traffic. Education lead generation SEO chases intent — students researching programs and institutions seeking qualified inquiries. Your architecture must serve both audiences without diluting conversion paths or compliance requirements.</p><h2>Map Intent to Page Types</h2><p>Informational queries belong in blog clusters that link to commercial service pages. High-intent program searches need dedicated landing pages with clear CTAs, privacy disclosures, and short qualification forms. Keep enrollment pages within three clicks of your homepage and primary navigation hubs.</p><h2>Technical Foundations That Support Leads</h2><p>Fast load times, mobile-first layouts, canonical URLs, and structured data (Organization, Service, FAQPage) help search engines understand your site while building trust with prospective students. Pair every organic landing page with conversion tracking so SEO performance ties directly to cost-per-start.</p><h2>Measure What Enrollment Teams Care About</h2><p>Track organic sessions, form submissions, lead quality scores, and start rate by landing page — not just keyword rankings. SEO wins in education when search visibility feeds a measurable enrollment funnel.</p>', 'Education Lead Generation SEO: The Complete Guide for 2026', 'How education marketers combine search visibility with consent-based lead capture — from keyword intent to enrollment-ready inquiries.', 'trash', 'open', 'open', '', 'education-lead-generation-seo-guide__trashed', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:55:45', '2026-06-16 20:55:45', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/education-lead-generation-seo-guide/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('83', '0', '2026-06-16 20:49:31', '2026-06-16 20:49:31', '<h2>What Is a Topic Cluster?</h2><p>A topic cluster centers on one pillar page covering a broad subject — like education lead generation or nursing pathways — supported by deeper articles on subtopics. Every cluster page links back to the pillar, and the pillar links out to each spoke. This structure signals topical authority to search engines.</p><h2>Choose Pillars Around Enrollment Goals</h2><p>Start with two or three pillars tied to revenue: student recruitment, program discovery, and institutional partnerships. Avoid thin tag archives; each hub should be a genuinely useful overview that routes readers to specific next steps.</p><h2>Internal Links Are the Architecture</h2><p>URL folders help, but contextual internal links do the heavy lifting. Place links high in the body content, use descriptive anchor text, and connect informational posts to commercial pages where intent shifts from research to inquiry.</p><h2>Grow Clusters Over Time</h2><p>Publish one pillar, add three to five cluster articles, then audit monthly for orphan pages. Update hub pages whenever new content goes live so search crawlers and users always find your latest resources.</p>', 'Topic Clusters for Higher Education SEO: Pillar Pages That Rank', 'Build topical authority with pillar pages and cluster content — the hub-and-spoke model for higher education websites.', 'trash', 'open', 'open', '', 'topic-clusters-for-higher-education-seo__trashed', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:55:45', '2026-06-16 20:55:45', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/topic-clusters-for-higher-education-seo/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('84', '0', '2026-06-16 20:49:31', '2026-06-16 20:49:31', '<h2>One Offer Per Page</h2><p>High-converting education landing pages focus on a single program, partnership offer, or audience segment. Remove distracting navigation where possible and align the headline with the search query or ad that brought the visitor.</p><h2>Above-the-Fold Clarity</h2><p>Within five seconds, visitors should know who the page is for, what they receive, and what action to take. Pair a keyword-focused H1 with a benefit-driven subhead, social proof near the form, and a visible CTA above the fold.</p><h2>Form Design for Conversion and Compliance</h2><p>Reduce fields to what you need for first contact — name, email, and one qualifier. Link to your privacy policy, disclose TCPA consent where required, and route submissions directly to your CRM with source attribution via UTM parameters.</p><h2>SEO Elements That Do Not Hurt Conversion</h2><p>Add meta titles, descriptions, FAQ schema, and internal links from related blog content. These improve discoverability without cluttering the conversion path. Test headline, CTA copy, and form length continuously to improve submission rate.</p>', 'Landing Page SEO for Education Leads: Structure That Converts', 'Structure enrollment landing pages for search visibility and lead conversion — hero, proof, form, and FAQ in the right order.', 'trash', 'open', 'open', '', 'landing-page-seo-for-education-leads__trashed', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:55:45', '2026-06-16 20:55:45', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/landing-page-seo-for-education-leads/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('85', '0', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '<h2>Internal Links Distribute Authority</h2><p>Every internal link helps search engines discover pages and signals which URLs matter most. On university and education marketing sites, priority targets are service pages, program hubs, and contact forms — not just the homepage.</p><h2>Link From Strong Pages to Weak Ones</h2><p>Identify pages with the most backlinks or organic traffic and add contextual links from those pages to high-priority enrollment URLs. Place links in the main body content, not only footers, and use anchor text that reflects the destination topic.</p><h2>Build Hub-and-Spoke Pathways</h2><p>Pillar pages should link to every cluster article; each cluster article should link back to its pillar and to one or two related siblings. Connect informational content to commercial pages when the reader is ready to take the next step.</p><h2>Audit Monthly</h2><p>Find orphan pages with no internal links, fix broken anchors, and reduce click depth for important URLs. A monthly internal link review prevents authority drift and keeps new blog content indexed quickly.</p>', 'Internal Linking for University SEO: Pass Authority to Enrollment Pages', 'Pass link authority to priority enrollment pages with strategic internal linking — contextual anchors, hub pages, and cluster cross-links.', 'trash', 'open', 'open', '', 'internal-linking-strategies-for-university-seo__trashed', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/internal-linking-strategies-for-university-seo/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('86', '0', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '<h2>Why Education SEO Is Different</h2><p>Generic SEO chases traffic. Education lead generation SEO chases intent — students researching programs and institutions seeking qualified inquiries. Your architecture must serve both audiences without diluting conversion paths or compliance requirements.</p><h2>Map Intent to Page Types</h2><p>Informational queries belong in blog clusters that link to commercial service pages. High-intent program searches need dedicated landing pages with clear CTAs, privacy disclosures, and short qualification forms. Keep enrollment pages within three clicks of your homepage and primary navigation hubs.</p><h2>Technical Foundations That Support Leads</h2><p>Fast load times, mobile-first layouts, canonical URLs, and structured data (Organization, Service, FAQPage) help search engines understand your site while building trust with prospective students. Pair every organic landing page with conversion tracking so SEO performance ties directly to cost-per-start.</p><h2>Measure What Enrollment Teams Care About</h2><p>Track organic sessions, form submissions, lead quality scores, and start rate by landing page — not just keyword rankings. SEO wins in education when search visibility feeds a measurable enrollment funnel.</p>', 'Education Lead Generation SEO: The Complete Guide for 2026', 'How education marketers combine search visibility with consent-based lead capture — from keyword intent to enrollment-ready inquiries.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '82-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '', '82', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=86', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('87', '0', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '<h2>What Is a Topic Cluster?</h2><p>A topic cluster centers on one pillar page covering a broad subject — like education lead generation or nursing pathways — supported by deeper articles on subtopics. Every cluster page links back to the pillar, and the pillar links out to each spoke. This structure signals topical authority to search engines.</p><h2>Choose Pillars Around Enrollment Goals</h2><p>Start with two or three pillars tied to revenue: student recruitment, program discovery, and institutional partnerships. Avoid thin tag archives; each hub should be a genuinely useful overview that routes readers to specific next steps.</p><h2>Internal Links Are the Architecture</h2><p>URL folders help, but contextual internal links do the heavy lifting. Place links high in the body content, use descriptive anchor text, and connect informational posts to commercial pages where intent shifts from research to inquiry.</p><h2>Grow Clusters Over Time</h2><p>Publish one pillar, add three to five cluster articles, then audit monthly for orphan pages. Update hub pages whenever new content goes live so search crawlers and users always find your latest resources.</p>', 'Topic Clusters for Higher Education SEO: Pillar Pages That Rank', 'Build topical authority with pillar pages and cluster content — the hub-and-spoke model for higher education websites.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '83-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '', '83', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=87', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('88', '0', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '<h2>One Offer Per Page</h2><p>High-converting education landing pages focus on a single program, partnership offer, or audience segment. Remove distracting navigation where possible and align the headline with the search query or ad that brought the visitor.</p><h2>Above-the-Fold Clarity</h2><p>Within five seconds, visitors should know who the page is for, what they receive, and what action to take. Pair a keyword-focused H1 with a benefit-driven subhead, social proof near the form, and a visible CTA above the fold.</p><h2>Form Design for Conversion and Compliance</h2><p>Reduce fields to what you need for first contact — name, email, and one qualifier. Link to your privacy policy, disclose TCPA consent where required, and route submissions directly to your CRM with source attribution via UTM parameters.</p><h2>SEO Elements That Do Not Hurt Conversion</h2><p>Add meta titles, descriptions, FAQ schema, and internal links from related blog content. These improve discoverability without cluttering the conversion path. Test headline, CTA copy, and form length continuously to improve submission rate.</p>', 'Landing Page SEO for Education Leads: Structure That Converts', 'Structure enrollment landing pages for search visibility and lead conversion — hero, proof, form, and FAQ in the right order.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '84-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '2026-06-16 20:49:32', '', '84', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=88', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('89', '0', '2026-06-16 20:49:33', '2026-06-16 20:49:33', '<h2>Internal Links Distribute Authority</h2><p>Every internal link helps search engines discover pages and signals which URLs matter most. On university and education marketing sites, priority targets are service pages, program hubs, and contact forms — not just the homepage.</p><h2>Link From Strong Pages to Weak Ones</h2><p>Identify pages with the most backlinks or organic traffic and add contextual links from those pages to high-priority enrollment URLs. Place links in the main body content, not only footers, and use anchor text that reflects the destination topic.</p><h2>Build Hub-and-Spoke Pathways</h2><p>Pillar pages should link to every cluster article; each cluster article should link back to its pillar and to one or two related siblings. Connect informational content to commercial pages when the reader is ready to take the next step.</p><h2>Audit Monthly</h2><p>Find orphan pages with no internal links, fix broken anchors, and reduce click depth for important URLs. A monthly internal link review prevents authority drift and keeps new blog content indexed quickly.</p>', 'Internal Linking for University SEO: Pass Authority to Enrollment Pages', 'Pass link authority to priority enrollment pages with strategic internal linking — contextual anchors, hub pages, and cluster cross-links.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '85-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:49:33', '2026-06-16 20:49:33', '', '85', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=89', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('90', '1', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Enrollment Challenge U.S. Universities Face</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Empty seats in high-demand programs still happen when marketing generates volume without enrollment intent. Nursing cohorts, online business degrees, and adult learner pathways require sustained inquiry flow - but generic lead lists and shared data purchases often fill CRMs with contacts who never answer, lack prerequisites, or enrolled with a competitor yesterday.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>U.S. institutions operate under tightening budgets, compliance scrutiny, and regional competition for the same student populations. Enrollment leaders need partners who understand program economics, advisor capacity, and the difference between an inquiry and a start.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Higher Learning Marketers was built to close that gap - connecting accredited universities and colleges with students who have already expressed interest in specific programs and provided explicit consent to be contacted.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How the HLM Partnership Model Works</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We manage targeted campaigns across nursing, business, and career-focused pathways nationwide. Prospective students discover programs through educational content and structured inquiry forms. We verify contact details, capture program interest and readiness signals, and deliver leads directly to your enrollment team or CRM integration.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>HLM inquiries are not recycled lists sold simultaneously to a dozen competing schools. Students engage with Higher Learning Marketers because they want guidance connecting to accredited institutions that match their goals, schedule, and location preferences.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Partners define geography, program mix, volume expectations, and delivery format. We scale campaigns toward your enrollment targets while maintaining consent documentation suitable for TCPA-aligned outreach.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Makes HLM Leads Different From Bulk Purchases</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Every inquiry includes opt-in consent, program-match metadata, and context advisors need for a productive first conversation - preferred start date, prior education, modality interest, and stated career goals where captured.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our partners report higher contact rates and stronger application progression compared with traditional list buying because students initiated the relationship. Quality reduces wasted advisor hours and improves cost-per-start even when CPL appears higher at the top of the funnel.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We align reporting with enrollment KPIs - not vanity metrics. Review contact rates, qualification rates, and downstream conversion with your account team and adjust targeting collaboratively.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Programs and Audiences We Support</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Higher Learning Marketers supports nursing pathways including RN, BSN, and MSN interest segments; business and professional degrees; and career-focused programs designed for working adults returning to school across the United States.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Campaign creative and qualification flows segment traditional students and adult learners so messaging reflects realistic schedules, transfer credit scenarios, and employer tuition benefits where relevant.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Whether you need volume for a flagship campus program or targeted online cohorts in specific states, we tailor delivery to admissions capacity and clinical or residency constraints that generic vendors ignore.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Compliance, Transparency, and Brand Protection</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Education marketing compliance is not optional. HLM forms disclose who will contact the student, link to our <a href=\"/privacy-policy/\">privacy policy</a>, and capture express consent before delivery to partner institutions. This reduces regulatory risk compared with opaque third-party co-reg paths.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Brand protection matters too. Students who trust the inquiry process engage more willingly with advisors. Aggressive list buying erodes trust when multiple universities call the same contact within hours.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our consent-first architecture supports defensible outreach for enrollment teams and general counsel reviewing vendor relationships.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Partner With Higher Learning Marketers</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If empty seats, rising acquisition costs, or weak vendor performance are limiting growth, a quality-first partnership may outperform scaling low-cost lists. Higher Learning Marketers combines full-funnel campaign management with enrollment-aligned reporting.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Explore our <a href=\"/services/\">lead generation services</a> or <a href=\"/contact-us/\">request a consultation</a> to discuss geography, program priorities, expected inquiry volume, and integration with your CRM. We help U.S. universities fill programs with students ready for the next step.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Onboarding and Integration With Your Enrollment Stack</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>HLM onboarding begins with program priorities, geography, modality constraints, and CRM delivery preferences. We configure real-time lead routing fields your advisors need on first contact - program interest, consent timestamp, preferred start, and education history where captured.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Integration support reduces manual CSV handling that delays speed-to-contact. Faster delivery preserves inquiry freshness and improves measurable conversion.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Partners receive reporting aligned to enrollment stages so marketing and admissions share a single view of performance.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Long-Term Partnership Versus One-Off Volume Spikes</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Sustainable enrollment growth favors consistent inquiry flow tuned to advisor capacity rather than episodic volume spikes that overwhelm teams and decay before contact.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>HLM adjusts targeting as your program mix evolves - new cohorts, expanded states, or shifted emphasis toward adult learners.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Long-term partners benefit from cumulative learning about which messages and qualification flows produce starts in their specific markets.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Operational Excellence Across the Enrollment Funnel</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Operational excellence separates institutions that convert inquiries into starts from those that accumulate CRM records without census impact. Weekly cross-functional reviews during application cycles surface bottlenecks - slow document processing, unclear financial aid answers, or advisor gaps during peak inquiry windows - before melt erodes ROI.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Document playbooks for first contact, qualification, and handoff between marketing-sourced inquiries and program-specific advisors. Consistency improves measurement and student experience alike.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Technology should serve the playbook: automated routing, SLA alerts, and source-level dashboards make problems visible early rather than at census.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'How Higher Learning Marketers Helps Universities Fill Programs With Qualified Students', 'How Higher Learning Marketers helps U.S. universities fill nursing, business, and career programs with consent-based, pre-qualified student inquiries.', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'how-hlm-helps-universities-fill-programs', '', '', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/how-hlm-helps-universities-fill-programs/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('91', '1', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">You Should Not Navigate Program Selection Alone</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Choosing a college or career program is a major decision - especially for working adults balancing employment, family, and long-term financial goals. The U.S. higher education landscape includes thousands of accredited options across campus, online, and hybrid formats. Sorting through prerequisites, transfer credits, licensure rules, and tuition models quickly becomes overwhelming without guidance.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Higher Learning Marketers exists to simplify that search. We connect prospective students with accredited institutions and program pathways aligned to stated interests - nursing, business, health sciences, and professional degrees offered by partner universities and colleges nationwide.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our role is not to pressure you into a single school. We help you understand options, compare formats, and initiate conversations with institutions that fit your goals on your timeline.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How the HLM Student Experience Works</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Students typically begin with educational content that clarifies program types - for example, RN versus BSN pathways, accelerated options for career changers, or business concentrations tied to industry demand. When you are ready, structured inquiry forms capture your program interests, location preferences, and contact details with clear consent language.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>An advisor reviews your submission and matches you with relevant partner institutions. You control which schools you engage - there is no obligation to enroll simply because you requested information.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Forms explain who will contact you and how your data is used, with access to our <a href=\"/privacy-policy/\">privacy policy</a> for full details on retention and rights.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who HLM Serves Across the United States</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We support traditional students exploring first degrees, working adults returning through evening or online formats, and career changers pursuing accelerated pathways. Nursing and healthcare programs remain among the most requested areas, alongside business and professional studies.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Partner institutions include career-focused colleges such as Berkeley College and other accredited providers offering campus and online attendance across multiple states. Program availability varies by location and licensure requirements - advisors clarify what applies to your situation.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you are comparing nursing programs specifically, our blog resources on choosing pathways and online versus campus formats complement personalized guidance.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What to Expect After You Submit an Inquiry</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>After you submit a form, expect contact from an advisor or partner institution within a reasonable window - often within one business day during standard hours. Prepare questions about start dates, transfer credits, financial aid, and schedule format so conversations are productive.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>You may speak with more than one school if multiple programs fit your criteria. Treat each conversation as fact-finding: ask about accreditation, graduate outcomes, clinical or internship requirements, and total cost of attendance.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>There is no fee to students for HLM matching services. Tuition and financial aid are arranged directly with institutions you choose to pursue.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tips for a Successful Program Search</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Define your non-negotiables before outreach: modality, maximum commute, licensure state, budget, and timeline to start. Share these upfront so advisors avoid mismatched recommendations.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Gather transcripts and employment history early if you expect transfer credit or prior learning assessment. Adult learners save time when documents are ready before application deadlines.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Compare programs on outcomes - NCLEX pass rates for nursing, employment rates for career degrees - not marketing slogans alone.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ready to Find Your Program?</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Whether you are exploring your first degree or advancing an established career, Higher Learning Marketers helps you move from research to informed conversations with accredited institutions.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><a href=\"/contact-us/\">Start your inquiry today</a> to connect with programs built for your future, or browse our blog for additional guidance on nursing pathways, adult learner applications, and enrollment planning across the United States.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Privacy and Control Over Your Information</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Students maintain control after inquiry. You choose which institutions to engage, ask questions about data use, and can reference our privacy policy for retention and sharing details.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>HLM never sells student information as a anonymous list to unrelated third parties for unrelated marketing. Matching services connect you to accredited education pathways based on stated interest.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you are not ready to speak with schools immediately, you can still use blog resources to compare programs before submitting a form.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Making the Most of Advisor Conversations</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Prepare a short list of questions before calls: accreditation, total cost, schedule format, transfer policies, and licensure outcomes where applicable.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Take notes during conversations and compare institutions on the same criteria rather than relying on memory across multiple calls.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Follow up promptly when schools request documents - adult learners often lose momentum when application steps linger unfinished.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Operational Excellence Across the Enrollment Funnel</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Operational excellence separates institutions that convert inquiries into starts from those that accumulate CRM records without census impact. Weekly cross-functional reviews during application cycles surface bottlenecks - slow document processing, unclear financial aid answers, or advisor gaps during peak inquiry windows - before melt erodes ROI.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Document playbooks for first contact, qualification, and handoff between marketing-sourced inquiries and program-specific advisors. Consistency improves measurement and student experience alike.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Technology should serve the playbook: automated routing, SLA alerts, and source-level dashboards make problems visible early rather than at census.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'How Students Find the Right College Program With Higher Learning Marketers', 'How students use Higher Learning Marketers to compare accredited U.S. college programs and connect with schools that fit their career goals and schedule.', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'how-students-find-the-right-program-with-hlm', '', '', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/how-students-find-the-right-program-with-hlm/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('92', '1', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Not All Education Leads Are Equal</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Premium education lead generation means delivering inquiries institutions can actually enroll - not raw contact data from questionable sources. Across the U.S. higher education market, universities face the same tension: marketing demands volume while enrollment leaders need starts in priority programs.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Higher Learning Marketers has spent more than a decade refining a model built on intent, consent, and program fit. Premium, in our definition, is measurable downstream - contact rates, qualification, applications, and starts - not a label attached to any list with a higher price tag.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Institutions paying for premium should expect transparency into sourcing, compliance language, exclusivity norms, and reporting tied to enrollment KPIs.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Our Full-Funnel Approach</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We manage the path from awareness to inquiry: targeted content, program-specific landing experiences, multi-step qualification forms, TCPA-compliant consent capture, and real-time delivery to your CRM or advisor queue.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Creative and form logic segment audiences - nursing versus business, adult learner versus traditional - so students self-qualify before outreach begins. This reduces advisor time spent on mismatched records.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Campaign optimization prioritizes sources and messages that produce starts, not just form fills. Weekly reviews with partners align spend and targeting with admissions capacity.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who We Serve in the U.S. Higher Education Market</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our partners include universities, colleges, and accredited program providers seeking consent-based inquiries across nursing, business, and career-focused pathways. We support campus, online, and hybrid modalities with geography and licensure constraints respected in targeting.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Premium delivery includes documented opt-in, program interest metadata, and support for integration with common enrollment CRMs. We scale volume to partner goals without sacrificing compliance architecture.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Explore how premium differs from commodity list buying in our related resources on <a href=\"/services/\">lead generation services</a> and lead quality fundamentals for enrollment teams.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Compliance as a Premium Requirement</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>TCPA-aligned telephonic outreach requires express consent with clear disclosure of who will call or text. Premium providers document that consent per inquiry and avoid recycled records lacking provenance.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>HLM forms link to our <a href=\"/privacy-policy/\">privacy policy</a>, name participating institutions, and capture affirmative student action - not pre-checked boxes buried in unrelated contests.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Compliance protects students and institutions. General counsel and enrollment leaders increasingly reject vendors who cannot produce consent artifacts on request.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Results That Matter: Enrollment, Not Clicks</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Premium lead generation should improve cost-per-start even when CPL rises. Partners choose Higher Learning Marketers because our inquiries convert at higher rates - students chose to engage and know why you are calling.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We report beyond top-of-funnel metrics wherever data allows: contact, qualification, application progression, and melt indicators. Accountability separates premium partnerships from transactional list purchases.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If your institution is evaluating vendors or rebuilding acquisition strategy, <a href=\"/contact-us/\">contact Higher Learning Marketers</a> to discuss enrollment targets, program mix, and expected ROI framing.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Choose Quality Over Commodity Volume</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Commodity leads commoditize your brand - duplicate calls, frustrated prospects, and advisors burning out on bad data. Premium inquiry generation invests in trust at capture so enrollment conversations start productively.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Higher Learning Marketers delivers that standard for U.S. universities and colleges ready to align marketing spend with starts. Request a consultation and compare our consent-based model to your current funnel performance.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How Premium Differs From Commodity List Brokers</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Commodity brokers optimize for record volume and resale across competing buyers. Premium partners optimize for documented consent, program alignment, and downstream conversion accountability.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Ask any vendor to show the exact user journey from first click to form submit. Premium providers welcome scrutiny; commodity sellers often deflect.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Price per record alone is misleading when contact rates differ by double digits.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Evaluating Premium Partnerships on Your Campus</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Pilot premium inquiry flows with defined KPIs - contact within 24 hours, qualification rate, application start - before committing full-term volume.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Compare pilot cohorts against historical sources with similar program targets, not against unrelated campaigns.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Higher Learning Marketers supports structured pilots for U.S. institutions evaluating a shift from list buying to consent-based generation.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Operational Excellence Across the Enrollment Funnel</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Operational excellence separates institutions that convert inquiries into starts from those that accumulate CRM records without census impact. Weekly cross-functional reviews during application cycles surface bottlenecks - slow document processing, unclear financial aid answers, or advisor gaps during peak inquiry windows - before melt erodes ROI.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Document playbooks for first contact, qualification, and handoff between marketing-sourced inquiries and program-specific advisors. Consistency improves measurement and student experience alike.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Technology should serve the playbook: automated routing, SLA alerts, and source-level dashboards make problems visible early rather than at census.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Continuous Improvement for U.S. Enrollment Teams</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Treat each enrollment cycle as a learning iteration. Compare source-level contact, application, and start rates; retain messaging that performs; pause spend that underperforms despite favorable CPL.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Invest savings into durable assets - content libraries, advisor training, and referral partnerships - that compound performance across terms rather than resetting with each vendor contract.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Partners like Higher Learning Marketers align with continuous improvement through consent-based inquiry delivery and reporting tied to enrollment outcomes. Explore our <a href=\"/services/\">services</a> or <a href=\"/contact-us/\">contact us</a> to strengthen your next cycle.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Premium Education Lead Generation: What Higher Learning Marketers Delivers', 'Premium education lead generation from Higher Learning Marketers - consent-based inquiries, TCPA-aligned capture, and enrollment outcomes for U.S. schools.', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'premium-education-lead-generation-hlm', '', '', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/premium-education-lead-generation-hlm/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('93', '1', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Compliance Is Not Optional in Education Marketing</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Universities face increasing scrutiny over how student data is collected, shared, and used for telephonic and text outreach. Regulatory frameworks including the Telephone Consumer Protection Act (TCPA) impose meaningful constraints on contact without express consent. Enrollment teams cannot treat compliance as a back-office concern separate from vendor selection.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Higher Learning Marketers built its platform on consent-first principles. Every lead we deliver includes documented opt-in from the student before any partner institution initiates contact.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Consent-based lead generation protects students from unwanted outreach and protects institutions from reputational and legal risk tied to weak data sourcing.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Consent-Based Means at HLM</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our forms clearly state who will contact the student, which types of programs are involved, and how information will be used. Students actively submit inquiries through Higher Learning Marketers - they are not pulled silently from unrelated databases or sweepstakes funnels without meaningful disclosure.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Consent language is plain, visible, and paired with access to our <a href=\"/privacy-policy/\">privacy policy</a> detailing retention, sharing, and student rights.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We retain artifacts supporting each inquiry so partners can demonstrate lawful basis for outreach during internal audits or student inquiries.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">TCPA and Data Privacy Alignment</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>TCPA requirements for autodialed calls and texts to mobile numbers demand express written consent in many contexts. Education vendors who rely on recycled or co-regulated records often struggle to produce defensible documentation when challenged.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>HLM aligns capture flows with TCPA expectations and GDPR-aligned practices where applicable for data handling transparency. Institutions reduce vendor risk when partnering with providers designed for scrutiny rather than speed-only list aggregation.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Privacy-forward capture also improves contact rates - students who understand why you are calling engage more often than those surprised by unexpected outreach.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Universities Choose Consent-Based Partners</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>General counsel and compliance officers increasingly participate in marketing vendor approvals. Consent-based inquiry generation simplifies those reviews with clear form screenshots, policy links, and per-lead opt-in records.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Enrollment benefits alongside compliance: advisors begin conversations with willing prospects who expect contact. Mismatch and hostility drop compared with cold list campaigns.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Brand trust compounds over time. Students who have positive first-touch experiences with transparent forms refer peers and complete applications at higher rates.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Contrast With Shared Lists and Opaque Sourcing</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Shared lead lists sold to multiple competing universities produce duplicate outreach that trains prospects to ignore calls. Opaque sourcing - where institutions cannot trace how a record was captured - creates compliance gaps that surface during audits or complaints.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Consent-based models reject those practices by design. Higher Learning Marketers delivers inquiries tied to identifiable capture events with program context.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>When evaluating alternatives, ask vendors to produce sample consent language and inquiry paths before signing volume commitments.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Trust Benefits Everyone in the Funnel</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Students trust Higher Learning Marketers because we are transparent about matching services and partner institutions. Universities trust us because our leads are defensible and aligned with enrollment quality goals.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If compliance and quality both matter to your enrollment strategy, explore our <a href=\"/services/\">consent-based lead generation services</a> or <a href=\"/contact-us/\">contact our team</a> to review capture flows, documentation, and partnership fit.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Document Retention and Audit Readiness</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Institutions should retain consent artifacts alongside CRM records for defensible outreach. HLM maintains capture documentation partners can reference during internal reviews.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>When students ask how their data was obtained, advisors should answer clearly with consent source and date - reducing complaint escalation.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Audit readiness is increasingly part of vendor selection scorecards alongside CPL.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Student Experience and Ethical Marketing</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Ethical education marketing respects student autonomy. Consent-based capture aligns business goals with that principle - willing conversations convert better than ambush outreach.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Universities promoting ethical recruitment strengthen brand among community partners, employers, and alumni referrers.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Consent-first architecture supports both compliance officers and enrollment leaders pursuing sustainable growth.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Operational Excellence Across the Enrollment Funnel</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Operational excellence separates institutions that convert inquiries into starts from those that accumulate CRM records without census impact. Weekly cross-functional reviews during application cycles surface bottlenecks - slow document processing, unclear financial aid answers, or advisor gaps during peak inquiry windows - before melt erodes ROI.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Document playbooks for first contact, qualification, and handoff between marketing-sourced inquiries and program-specific advisors. Consistency improves measurement and student experience alike.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Technology should serve the playbook: automated routing, SLA alerts, and source-level dashboards make problems visible early rather than at census.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Continuous Improvement for U.S. Enrollment Teams</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Treat each enrollment cycle as a learning iteration. Compare source-level contact, application, and start rates; retain messaging that performs; pause spend that underperforms despite favorable CPL.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Invest savings into durable assets - content libraries, advisor training, and referral partnerships - that compound performance across terms rather than resetting with each vendor contract.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Partners like Higher Learning Marketers align with continuous improvement through consent-based inquiry delivery and reporting tied to enrollment outcomes. Explore our <a href=\"/services/\">services</a> or <a href=\"/contact-us/\">contact us</a> to strengthen your next cycle.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Practical Next Steps for Your Institution</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Schedule a working session with marketing, admissions, financial aid, and compliance stakeholders to review current inquiry sources, consent documentation, and stage-level conversion rates. Shared visibility prevents blame cycles and accelerates fixes.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Identify one underperforming channel to pause and one high-potential channel to test with structured KPIs this term. Small disciplined experiments beat broad budget swings.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>When you are ready to add or replace a vendor, prioritize partners who document consent, align with program fit, and report beyond form fills - the standard Higher Learning Marketers brings to U.S. university partnerships every day.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Why Higher Learning Marketers Uses Consent-Based, TCPA-Compliant Lead Generation', 'Consent-based education leads from Higher Learning Marketers: TCPA-aligned capture, transparent forms, and audit-ready documentation for U.S. universities.', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'consent-based-education-leads-hlm', '', '', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '2026-06-18 18:21:40', '', '0', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/consent-based-education-leads-hlm/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('94', '1', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '<h2>The Enrollment Challenge Universities Face</h2><p>Empty seats cost revenue. Generic lead lists waste advisor time. Higher Learning Marketers was built to solve this — connecting accredited institutions with students who have already expressed interest in specific programs and given explicit consent to be contacted.</p><h2>How Our Partnership Model Works</h2><p>We run targeted campaigns across nursing, business, and career-focused pathways. Prospective students discover programs through our content and inquiry forms. We verify contact details, capture program interest, and deliver leads directly to your enrollment team — not a shared list sold to competitors.</p><h2>What Makes HLM Leads Different</h2><p>Every inquiry includes consent documentation, program-match data, and readiness signals like preferred start date. Our partners report higher contact rates and better start outcomes compared to bulk purchased lists because students chose to reach out.</p><h2>Partner With Us</h2><p>Whether you need volume for a flagship program or targeted adult-learner campaigns, Higher Learning Marketers scales delivery to your enrollment goals. Request a consultation to discuss geography, program mix, and expected inquiry volume.</p>', 'How Higher Learning Marketers Helps Universities Fill Programs With Qualified Students', 'How Higher Learning Marketers partners with universities and colleges to deliver pre-qualified, consent-based student inquiries that convert to enrollment.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '90-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '', '90', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=94', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('95', '1', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '<h2>You Should Not Navigate This Alone</h2><p>Choosing a college or career program is a major decision — especially for working adults balancing jobs, family, and education goals. Higher Learning Marketers exists to connect you with accredited institutions that match your interests, schedule, and career path.</p><h2>How We Help Students</h2><p>Through our platform you can explore nursing, business, and professional programs offered by partner universities. Our advisors help you understand options, compare pathways like RN versus BSN, and connect directly with schools that fit your goals.</p><h2>What to Expect When You Inquire</h2><p>Submitting a form takes minutes. An advisor reviews your program interest and matches you with relevant institutions. There is no obligation — you control the conversation and choose which schools to engage.</p><h2>Ready to Find Your Program?</h2><p>Whether you are a first-time student or a working professional ready to advance your career, Higher Learning Marketers simplifies the search. Start your inquiry today and connect with programs built for your future.</p>', 'How Students Find the Right College Program With Higher Learning Marketers', 'How prospective students use Higher Learning Marketers to compare programs, connect with accredited institutions, and take the next step toward enrollment.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '91-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '2026-06-16 20:55:46', '', '91', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=95', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('96', '1', '2026-06-16 20:55:47', '2026-06-16 20:55:47', '<h2>Not All Education Leads Are Equal</h2><p>Premium education lead generation means delivering inquiries institutions can actually enroll — not raw contact data from questionable sources. Higher Learning Marketers has spent over a decade refining a model built on intent, consent, and program fit.</p><h2>Our Full-Funnel Approach</h2><p>We manage the complete path from awareness to inquiry: targeted content, multi-step qualification forms, TCPA-compliant consent capture, and real-time delivery to your CRM or enrollment team. You receive students who know what program they want and have agreed to hear from you.</p><h2>Who We Serve</h2><p>Our partners include universities, colleges, and accredited program providers across the United States. We support nursing pathways, business degrees, and career-focused programs for both traditional and adult learners.</p><h2>Results That Matter</h2><p>Institutions partner with HLM because our leads convert. We focus on cost-per-start, not cost-per-click. Explore our services or contact us to discuss how premium lead generation can support your enrollment targets.</p>', 'Premium Education Lead Generation: What Higher Learning Marketers Delivers', 'What premium education lead generation means at Higher Learning Marketers — quality over volume, compliance, and proven results for institutions.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '92-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:55:47', '2026-06-16 20:55:47', '', '92', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=96', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('97', '1', '2026-06-16 20:55:47', '2026-06-16 20:55:47', '<h2>Compliance Is Not Optional in Education Marketing</h2><p>Universities face increasing scrutiny over how student data is collected and used. Higher Learning Marketers built its platform on consent-first principles — every lead we deliver includes documented opt-in from the student before any institution makes contact.</p><h2>What Consent-Based Means in Practice</h2><p>Our forms clearly state who will contact the student, which programs are involved, and how data will be used. Students actively submit inquiries rather than being scraped from databases or purchased from third-party aggregators without their knowledge.</p><h2>TCPA and GDPR Alignment</h2><p>We follow TCPA requirements for telephonic contact and GDPR-aligned practices for data handling and privacy. Our privacy policy outlines retention, sharing, and student rights. Institutions that partner with us reduce compliance risk compared to vendors with opaque data sourcing.</p><h2>Trust Benefits Everyone</h2><p>Students trust us because we are transparent. Universities trust us because our leads are defensible. If compliance and quality matter to your enrollment strategy, Higher Learning Marketers is the partner built for both.</p>', 'Why Higher Learning Marketers Uses Consent-Based, TCPA-Compliant Lead Generation', 'Why Higher Learning Marketers built its entire lead generation model on explicit consent, TCPA compliance, and GDPR-aligned data practices.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '93-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-16 20:55:47', '2026-06-16 20:55:47', '', '93', 'https://higherlearningmarketers.com/?p=97', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
